WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page `GasPriceAutoPollPage.tsx` is a thin `PageContainer` (title + subtitle)
that wraps the shared `<GasPriceSettings />` component. The native `GasPriceSettings`
feature surface ALREADY EXISTS as its own parity unit (P4 feature view · 0206,
apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/GasPriceSettings*.swift) — a full @Observable
GasPriceSettingsModel + panel with the fuel-pump header, auto-poll toggle, poll-interval
select, current-price / last-polled cells, "Poll Now" action + EIA caption, and every
loading / empty / error / data + stale / offline state.

Per the Honesty Covenant "No predecessor bypass", this page therefore REUSES that
component rather than re-implementing it. `GasPriceAutoPollPage` is the SwiftUI parity of
the web PAGE WRAPPER: a HIG-native scaffold (ScrollView → page title + subtitle, web
`PageContainer`) that embeds the existing `GasPriceSettings(model:)`. No data logic is
duplicated; the gas-price price values are SI-free currency strings read from the API, so
no unit conversion applies (the ADR display-boundary rule is satisfied by the component's
own GasPriceFormat port). There are no charts and no map (manifest declares 0/0).

Navigation: the web route /gas-price maps 1:1 to AppRoute.gasPrice (new case, pathSegment
"gas-price", SF Symbol "fuelpump.fill", System sidebar group), so AppRouteParser resolves
it directly with NO alias — reachable + deep-linkable. route.gasPrice = "Gas Prices" (the
web Layout sidebar label). The only exhaustive AppRoute switches live in AppRoute.swift
(verified: the System-group cases are referenced only in AppRoute.swift + AppRouteParser),
so no other file needed a new case arm.

i18n: the two page-level parity strings resolve through the component's own localization
facade `GasPriceStrings.string("gas.title" / "gas.subtitle", <web English fallback>)` —
the verbatim web i18next keys (namespace "settings"), so a shared catalog resolves
identically across web + native. The pre-seeded `translation.gas.*` catalog keys back the
embedded panel. Zero hardcoded user-facing strings.

